 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504775,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Use the prime factorization method to find the LCM of 150, 240, and 462.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find the prime factorization of each number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"150 = 2 \\times 3 \\times {5^2}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"240 = {2^4} \\times 3 \\times 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"462 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7 \\times 11\"></span></p>\n<p>Make a table of each prime and the largest exponent for each prime.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>11</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exponent</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LCM is the product of each prime raised to the powers identified in the table.</p>\n<p>The LCM is <span data-math=\"{2^4} \\times 3 \\times {5^2} \\times 7 \\times 11 = 92,400\"></span>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "92,400"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
